WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.220
Good morning, John!

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:03.420
Paternity leave break. What am I doing here?

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:08.420
I pre-recorded this video because I have some things to tell you about VidCon...s. VidCons.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:09.340
Three of them.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:13.800
I think my favorite thing about being a YouTube creator is it let's me be on a stage and talk to you in real life.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.220
VidCon is one of the only times of year you get to get together and see each other.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.820
I don't want a TV show! I want to be a pioneer of something brand new.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:25.860
We should only be sharing our ideas in the environment that enables us to do that the best.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:30.840
Let go of the ego behind it and focus on what matters, which is reaching the audience.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.900
And nothing enables that like the internet.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:01:03.220
[music]

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:06.560
Hank: we come together at VidCon to immerse ourselves in the world of online video.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:11.300
To connect with our friends and our communities, and to capture and reflect the state of this ever changing

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:15.080
and thriving culture, and simply to celebrate.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.900
We are please to announce the VidCon: US will return to the Anaheim Convention Center

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.260
for another exceptional weekend: June 21-24.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:25.480
And, for the first time ever, VidCon is going global.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.260
VidCon: Europe will kick off April 8-9 in Amsterdam

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:32.680
with VidCon: Australia following on September 9-10 in Melbourne.

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:36.580
These are two cities that foster innovation and collaboration.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.360
They're cosmopolitan, friendly, and lively cities.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:42.800
And we're very excited to see how VidCon lives and breathes in these new homes.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:46.400
Tickets are officially available now for VidCon: US.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.980
VidCon: Europe and VidCon: Australia, I hope to see ya there!

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:54.040
[music]

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:55.900
Hank: I am so excited to be going to these things!

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.320
I have never been to Amsterdam.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:59.600
I have never been to the souther hemisphere.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:01.640
No Australia, no Sydney, no Melbourne, no anything.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:04.500
I will be at all three: Anaheim, Amsterdam, and Melbourne.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.800
John, you're only gonna be able to be at Anaheim.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:11.660
So I will just have to be both me and you for those people there, which I think I can pull off.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:13.380
I've been working on your signature, it's not complicated.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:16.920
Maybe you can like--you can Skype in for a Dear Hank and John. That'd be fun.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.120
I say without having asked you about that first.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.420
We're digging into the really interesting creator communities in these places,

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:25.680
but we will also be bringing creators from the US and the UK

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:30.160
We're so lucky at VidCon to be able to represent a diversity of creators and creations

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:33.500
and going international is a huge step in that direction for us.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.880
I'm really excited about it. I think it's gonna be a ton of fun.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:38.700
I apologize to you for coming back from leave temporarily

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:41.560
just to let most of you know about events that you're not gonna be able to be at.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:47.400
I feel very bad for all the people who live far away from these events, but now there are fewer of you!

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.960
For everybody who can come, I'm so excited to see you in Anaheim, Melbourne, and Amsterdam.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:54.500
John, thank you so much for taking care of this place

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:58.560
and for all of our guest hosts for taking care of this space while I've been gone.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:03.320
I don't know how it's gone because as I said, I pre-recorded this because I am on leave.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:07.160
Thanks for not burning the channel down, I assume, and I'll see you on Tuesday.

